 ```
 
+## Confining the files an agent reaches
+
+```sh
+deckcraft-cli mcp --automation-read-root ~/agent/in --automation-write-root ~/agent/out
+```
+
+The headless server's commands then open and insert files (presentations, outlines, pictures,
+audio and video) only from inside the read root, and save, export and render them to a file only
+inside the write root. Each flag is `--flag DIR` or `--flag=DIR`, given once; the folder must
+exist. A root left out grants no access of its kind (with only a read root, nothing can be saved to
+a file). Paths are made absolute and their links followed before they are compared by whole folder
+names (without regard to case on Windows), so `..`, a sibling with the same prefix or a link or
+junction out of the root is refused, with an `automation path rejected: …` or `automation
+filesystem access is not granted: …` error, and nothing is written outside. `--sample` is opened
+before the roots apply. The roots don't confine a running app: with `--connect` they are refused. A
+program that can change the folders while a command runs can still race the check; the roots keep
+an agent to the files it was given.
+
